{
  "name": "Signup Intake → CRM triage",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Take signups into Google Sheets with a Telegram triage step\n\nA generic intake door for inbound people, with or without a website. Every signup is stored, checked against your contact book, mailed a confirmation and announced on Telegram, where one tap marks it promoted or dismissed. It shows how anyone can capture inbound interest without writing a backend.\n\n### How it works\n1. Takes a signup from a webhook your site posts to, or from a form page n8n hosts for you.\n2. Shapes both into one record and looks the address up in the contact book.\n3. Appends the signup to its own sheet and writes the contact row.\n4. Sends a confirmation email whose text is rendered by your site.\n5. Alerts you on Telegram with the contact's current record and two buttons.\n6. Marks the signup promoted or dismissed when you tap one.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Give the signups sheet these headers: `email  first_name  surname  use_case  source  signup_timestamp  known_in_crm  status`\n- [ ] Connect a Google Sheets credential and pick the signups sheet or the contact book in each Sheets node\n- [ ] Connect a Telegram bot credential and set your chat ID in **Send Signup Alert**\n- [ ] Set the URL in **Render Email** to your confirmation-email endpoint and connect Gmail in **Send Confirmation Email**\n- [ ] Activate, then give the webhook's production URL to your site, or share the form URL\n\n[Project page](https://github.com/runfish5/micro-services/blob/main/projects/n8n/shared/README.md)",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0061-4061-8061-000000000061",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -460,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
